WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:06.873
Hello internet!

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.055
Hiya, how's it going?

00:00:09.055 --> 00:00:10.202
Are you asking me or the internet?

00:00:10.202 --> 00:00:11.150
I don' care about you,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:11.983
so I'm asking the internet.

00:00:11.983 --> 00:00:12.930
I assume they are fine,

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.620
because they are watching
The Slow Mo Guys video--

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.453
Big time.

00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:16.286
On the internet.

00:00:16.286 --> 00:00:17.807
Well, today we've got a
car airbag, haven't we?

00:00:17.807 --> 00:00:18.960
I was always amazed that,

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.238
when an airbag goes off in a
car, in the steering wheel,

00:00:21.238 --> 00:00:22.071
I thought:

00:00:22.071 --> 00:00:24.230
How does the airbag not hit
the driver in the face?--

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.690
Yes, just think of it as a big smack.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.286
How does it just deploy in his face?

00:00:27.286 --> 00:00:30.018
And it turns out airbags
deploy so immensely fast,

00:00:30.018 --> 00:00:32.470
that usually, they are
fully out and inflated

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.389
before the driver has even
moved from the impact.

00:00:35.389 --> 00:00:38.160
So let us see how fast that
really is by filming it

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.060
at two and a half thousand
frames a second in HD,

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.093
with a fan of flex.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:44.723
Got batteries, so yeah,

00:00:44.723 --> 00:00:45.556
I'm going to connect them up,

00:00:45.556 --> 00:00:47.230
so hopefully that would work,

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.198
but I'm a bit scared about
this one to be honest.

00:00:49.198 --> 00:00:50.298
All right Dan.

00:00:50.298 --> 00:00:52.203
Wear this for safety.

00:00:53.466 --> 00:00:54.299
I don't want--

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:57.813
I'm a bit scared!

00:00:57.813 --> 00:00:59.083
All right, go for it!

00:00:59.083 --> 00:00:59.916
What?

00:00:59.916 --> 00:01:01.189
Go for it!

00:01:04.691 --> 00:01:05.691
Bloody hell!

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:09.382
me!

00:01:09.382 --> 00:01:10.215
That was fast!

00:01:10.215 --> 00:01:11.048
Oh my god.

00:01:11.048 --> 00:01:11.883
Bloody heck.

00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:13.010
Did you see me jump?

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.162
No!

00:01:14.162 --> 00:01:17.079
I myself.

00:01:45.462 --> 00:01:46.295
Oh.

00:01:46.295 --> 00:01:47.128
Whoa!

00:01:47.128 --> 00:01:47.961
That's fast!

00:01:47.961 --> 00:01:48.794
That is so fast!

00:01:48.794 --> 00:01:50.388
Look at it flapping about!

00:01:50.388 --> 00:01:52.700
That's straight in your face!

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.139
Now you noticed the
airbags never just explode,

00:01:55.139 --> 00:01:58.230
because they are actually
vented at the back.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:01:59.063
See this here?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.241
The explosion puts air into a
bag that is not even sealed.

00:02:03.241 --> 00:02:04.074
Ah!

00:02:04.074 --> 00:02:05.950
So that air can leak out without the bag

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.330
just exploding form the pressure.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.163
Did not know that.

00:02:09.163 --> 00:02:09.996
Pretty cool, isn't it?

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:10.829
Yeah, it's pretty awesome.

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:11.830
Also, very hot!

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:12.970
Yeah, I felt that afterwards,

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:15.093
I've touched it and it
was actually really warm.

00:02:16.142 --> 00:02:17.420
All right, so we have a second airbag.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.253
Yep.

00:02:18.253 --> 00:02:20.880
That first one went off,
but you can't really--

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.713
Really.

00:02:21.713 --> 00:02:23.140
See any sort of scale of speed,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.460
we have got to try and drop something

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:26.720
next to this one, right?

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.760
Yeah, so you turn it right.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.850
So you drop something
as this one goes off.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:35.489
I see you are using a standard
procedure kitchen knife.

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:36.810
This would not be a slammer guys,

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:37.827
if we did not have the
completely incorrect

00:02:37.827 --> 00:02:39.293
equipment to use though.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.580
Ready?

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.413
Yeah.

00:02:44.413 --> 00:02:45.246
Yeah.

00:02:48.496 --> 00:02:49.329
Woo!

00:02:49.329 --> 00:02:50.162
Where did it go?

00:02:50.162 --> 00:02:51.314
me!

00:02:51.314 --> 00:02:52.147
Over there!

00:02:53.004 --> 00:02:54.260
By the tree!

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.023
Jesus Christ!

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.963
Holy crap!

00:02:58.963 --> 00:03:00.823
Oh my god!

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:44.060
Good lord!

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.680
Literally, that all happened so quickly,

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.089
I blinked, the airbag was over there,

00:03:48.089 --> 00:03:49.587
and the glass was about
30 meters over there.

00:03:49.587 --> 00:03:51.965
Why am I so confused as to
everything that is over there?

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.240
Hard to say, you just go like duff!

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.177
What happened?

00:03:54.177 --> 00:03:56.550
This was much bigger than the other one.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.962
It had a lot more volume to it, didn't it?

00:03:57.962 --> 00:03:58.795
Yeah, it was like...

00:03:58.795 --> 00:03:59.820
I guess you are further away from it--

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:00.782
It looked softer--

00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:01.615
